From b70c1d15de139b67c594a157461412281a44599c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikhil Gurram <nikhgurr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: RepAP 6G FH VAPs fail to come up after association with RootAP

wld_mld_firstUsableNeighLinkByFreq() used'> tgtFreq' 
which always elected the highest-frequency (6GHz) radio as
BH STA MLO primary anchor. On IPQ the 6GHz pdev is firmware-
designated as a scan radio (WMI_SCAN_RADIO_CAP_SCAN_RADIO), limited to
one vdev at a time. With the BH STA vdev already occupying that slot,
NL80211_CMD_ADD_LINK for wlan0.1 (6G FH AP) returned -EINVAL from the
ath12k single-vdev guard in mac.c. with this change lowest-frequency
(2.4GHz) radio is elected primary; 6GHz becomes an
AUXILIARY MLO link and its vdev slot is free for the FH AP.

Crash loop fix (wifiGen_hapd.c, wifiGen_fsm.c, wld.h): when the 6G FH
AP warm-add (ADD bss_config) fails, the old code called
s_schedNextAction(NEED_RESTART) which restarted the shared hostapd
group, killing the working 2G/5G FH VAPs in a crash loop. Replace with
a per-radio hapdWarmAddFailed flag: defer the retry via a 5-second
timer, exclude the failed radio from the cold-start conf aggregation,
and skip the "already started" early-return so the retry actually
re-attempts the warm-add.

Signed-off-by: Nikhil Gurram <nikhgurr@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 static bool s_hasRtmSchedState(T_Radio* pRad, wifiGen_fsmStates_e fsmAc) {
--- a/src/wld_mld.c
+++ b/src/wld_mld.c
@@ -762,9 +762,11 @@
         if(pRad == NULL) {
             continue;
         }
         if(wld_mld_isLinkUsable(pLink) &&
            (pRad->operatingFrequencyBand < SWL_FREQ_BAND_EXT_NONE) &&
-           ((tgtFreq == SWL_FREQ_BAND_EXT_NONE) || (pRad->operatingFrequencyBand > tgtFreq))) {
+           /* Prefer lowest-frequency band as BH STA primary anchor so 6GHz stays
+            * AUXILIARY and wlan0.1 remains free for 6G FH AP ADD_LINK. */
+           ((tgtFreq == SWL_FREQ_BAND_EXT_NONE) || (pRad->operatingFrequencyBand < tgtFreq))) {
             tgtLink = pLink;
             tgtFreq = pRad->operatingFrequencyBand;
         }
